-          "quote": "Suppose the stored entries of $B=\\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{pmatrix}$ have supplied exact rational encodings $a=p_a/q_a$, $b=p_b/q_b$, $c=p_c/q_c$, $d=p_d/q_d$, with integer numerators and positive integer denominators. Put $Q=q_aq_bq_cq_d$ and $A=p_a(Q/q_a)$, $B_0=p_b(Q/q_b)$, $C_0=p_c(Q/q_c)$, $D=p_d(Q/q_d)$. Compute the integer\n$$Z=(A-D)^2+4B_0C_0.$$\nIts integer sign is exactly [[def-exact-real-2x2-discriminant-sign-predicate]] and is found after finitely many exact integer operations. Finite binary floating values with their signed-integer/power-of-two encodings are a special case. This evaluator does not assume arbitrary stored real numbers have rational encodings. If an exact encoding or another terminating exact sign evaluator is unavailable, retain `schur-type-undecided`.",
