+            "quote": "For a real matrix $B=\\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{pmatrix}$, define its characteristic-polynomial discriminant by $\\Delta(B)=(a+d)^2-4(ad-bc)$. Define $\\operatorname{discSign}(B)$ to be $-1$, $0$, or $1$ according as the exact real number $\\Delta(B)$ is negative, zero, or positive. This is an exact mathematical predicate on the stored real entries, not an operation in the operationwise floating-point model. A computed procedure may report a sign only when its control predicate establishes this exact value; otherwise it reports undecided.",
