rix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{pmatrix}$; compute $s=\\operatorname{fl}(a+d)$ and $t=\\operatorname{fl}(\\operatorname{fl}(ad)-\\operatorname{fl}(bc))$ in that order, returning range-failure if an operation fails. Maintain a counter for each active block, reset it after any deflation in that block, and after $h$ consecutive sweeps without deflation consume that block's next declared exceptional shift or real quadratic. If the required table entry is absent, return stagnation-exhausted.\n4. Apply the corresponding implicit bulge chase from [[alg-exact-francis-hessenberg-qr-step]]. For the initial single-shift vector compute $x_1=\\operatorname{fl}(h_{11}-\\mu)$ and $x_i=h_{i1}$ for $i>1$. For the initial real double-shift vector, compute $u=He_1$, then $w=Hu$ by left-to-right rounded matrix-vector products, then $x=\\operatorname{fl}(\\operatorname{fl}(w-su)+te_1)$ componentwise. Compute only the first $r+1$ components from the Hessenberg support pattern; on range failure return the operation index and partial factors. For a chase at column $j$, use active indices $S=I_j$, target $x=H_{S,j}$, and trailing left panel $B=H_{S,\\{j+1,\\ldots,n\\}}$ with columns in increasing order. Call the real or complex formation routine, write the target tail zeros exactly, complete the two-sided update by the right-kernel order above on columns $S$, and append the exact reflector representation to $Q$. In the initial polynomial-vector step there is no matrix-target column; use the full active row panel for the left update and then apply the right update to its active columns. If the exact routine or its finite-precision realization returns bulge-chase-invariant-failure, return that status with the partial matrix and factors. Use [[lem-two-sided-scaled-householder-similarity-error]] to store the proved two-sided coefficient $\\alpha_{m_j}=a_{m_j}+b_{m_j}+a_{m_j}b_{m_j}$, with $a$ the target-overwrite coefficient or separate-block coefficient as actually used and $b$ the right separate-block co