+          "quote": "Input a real or complex square matrix $A\\in\\mathbb F^{n\\times n}$ with $n\\ge1$, a finite nonnegative deflation tolerance $\\tau$, a nonnegative integer sweep budget $N$, a positive integer stagnation period $h$, finite tables of finite exceptional shifts, optional exact rational/dyadic encodings of its stored real values, optionally a terminating exact evaluator of [[def-exact-real-2x2-discriminant-sign-predicate]], and optionally a terminating outward evaluator for nonnegative expressions and Frobenius norms. The outward evaluator's `upadd`, `upmul`, and `upsqrt` calls return finite nonnegative represented upper bounds for the exact sum, product, and square root, while `upnormF(X)` returns a finite represented upper bound for $\\|X\\|_F$; any call may instead return `unavailable`. In the declared scalar-cost model, each `upadd`, `upmul`, and `upsqrt` call has unit cost and `upnormF(X)` makes one pass over the entries of $X$ with a fixed number of such calls per real component. The evaluator acts only on certificate bookkeeping. A formation `breakdown` is propagated with the operation index and partial factors. Every scalar operation in the main procedure is evaluated in the operationwise model of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]]. Any invalid, overflow, or underflow operation in the main procedure returns range-failure with the operation index and partial factors.\n\nBefore every real or complex formation in steps 1 and 4, test the target vector componentwise for exact zero, including an external initial polynomial vector. If it is zero, mark the stage `identity`, copy all affected matrix entries unchanged, skip formation and both left and right updates, append the embedded identity $P_j=I$ to the product representation, and record $E_j=0$ and arithmetic coefficient $\\alpha_j=\\bar\\alpha_j=0$. Do not evaluate $P(v)$ or a stored-vector norm in this branch. For a matrix target its column is already ze